If-Else Statements in Ruby

Basic Syantx:
if condition
elsif condition
elsif condition
else
end


age = 18
if age >= 18
puts "You are an adult"
else
puts "You are a minor"
end

marks = 67

If marks are less than 25, it prints "Grade: F."
If marks are between 25 and 44 (inclusive), it prints "Grade: E."
If marks are between 45 and 49 (inclusive), it prints "Grade: D."
If marks are between 50 and 59 (inclusive), it prints "Grade: C."
If marks are between 60 and 69 (inclusive), it prints "Grade: B."
If marks are 70 or higher, it prints "Grade: A."
If marks are outside the valid range, it prints "Invalid marks entered."

marks = 25
if marks <= 25
	puts "Grade: F."
elsif marks >= 25 && marks <= 44
	puts "Grade: E."
elsif marks >= 45 && marks <= 49 
	puts "Grade: D."
elsif marks >= 50 && marks <= 59
	puts "Grade: C."
elsif marks >= 60 && marks <= 69
	puts "Grade: B."
elsif marks >= 70
	puts "Grade: A."
else 
	puts "Invalid marks entered."
end


Problem:
Write a Ruby program that takes a user's age as input and prints:
"Too young to vote" if age is less than 18
"Eligible to vote" if age is between 18 and 60 (inclusive)
"Senior citizen voter" if age is above 60

puts "Enter the age"
age = gets.chomp.to_i
if age < 18 
    puts "Too young to vote"
elsif age >= 18 && age <= 60
    puts "Eligible to vote"
else
    puts "Senior citizen voter"
end


